 (also (yam-use-fuel)
  (: _
   (yam-runtime-require (= (size types) (size keys))
    "Function argument count mismatch" group)
   (if (= i (size types)) (#)
    (: _
     (yam-runtime-require
      (yam-runtime-equal (. i types) (yam-runtime-child t (. i keys) group)
       group)
      "Function argument type mismatch" group)
     (yam-runtime-check-arguments types t keys (+ i 1) group))))))

# "Checking a function and capturing its environment

   Arguments extend a fresh scope. Outer bindings are captured explicitly and
   become reads from the resulting closure's capture object. The body
   determines the return type. A recursive group supplies expected
   signatures, which are checked fully before any function value from that
   group can run."

# "Functions retain their meaning as well as their executable code.

   A public function is [raw, captures]. The raw descriptor stores its
   debugging name, typed captures, typed parameters, semantic body, and VM
   function. Three private fields describe where a shared function group
   lives in the captures, the group's lexical bindings, and the offset of
   ordinary captured values.

   Native code uses compact numbered references into its immutable
   raw-function group. Checked expression compilation instead uses named
   lexical groups. Both are converted to ordinary function constants only
   when code is requested. The public Expr never contains a pointer,
   unchecked load, or opaque builtin."

